## Step 1: Define the Class

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  NEW CLASS                                              │
│  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────  │
│                                                         │
│  Name *          [ Consumer                      ]      │
│  Label           [ Consumer / Borrower           ]      │
│  Namespace       [ credit:          ▼            ]      │
│                                                         │
│  Parent Class    [ Search parent...           🔍 ]      │
│                    ↳ semantic search existing classes   │
│                                                         │
│  Description *   [ Individual about whom credit  ]      │
│                  [ information is compiled        ]      │
│                                                         │
│  Domain Tags     [ Credit ×] [ Fraud ×] [ +Add   ]      │
│                                                         │
│  Abstract?       [ No ▼ ]    Status  [ Draft ▼   ]      │
│                                                         │
│                            [ Save & Add Properties → ]  │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

**Key decisions at this step:**

- **Name + namespace** establishes the canonical identity
- **Parent class** enables inheritance — properties flow down
- **Abstract flag** means base class only, never directly mapped to a dataset
- **Description** is the seed for semantic search later

